NOTE: every SQL statement issued from Python went through db.py's q(), which appended it to this log at execution time (lines beginning "python3(db.py <tag>)"); shell-level ./q.sh calls logged themselves (lines beginning "sqlite3 -readonly DB"). Commands that read only this run directory (cat/sed/cut/grep/head on raw/ and *.tsv, ctx.py over raw/ dumps, wc) are not resource reads and were not logged one by one.
ELIDED: (1) Python heredoc and `python3 -c` bodies are logged by one-line description, not verbatim — the scripts that matter are kept on disk (heads.py, chapters.py, latamdocs.py, scopeA.py, scopeB.py, decades.py, controls.py, arch.py, glosscf.py, glosspa.py, lots.py, shares.py, precB.py, readdocs.py, verifyq.py, buildcoll.py, checkcoll.py, db.py, q.sh); the unsaved inline ones were: manifest-structure and post-1950-volume listing, JSON top-level/structure inspections (central-files, series-facts, collection-usage, decimal-class-labels, external-citation, presidential-library-catalog), pre-1906 countrySeries resolution, pre-1910 and 1910+ scope header listings (dept_instr.txt), the false-friend test, the cited-doc verification, the dated-cited and scope-range queries, the reading accounting, and the in-place overview/memo edits; their SQL is nonetheless logged verbatim via db.py. (2) params= values in db.py lines are truncated to 300 characters (the NEAR query text is in nearq.txt). (3) Commands over this run directory only (see NOTE) are not listed. (4) Outputs are not in this log; they are in the *.out / *.tsv files named in memo.md.
